/-!
# GanGrossPrasadUnitaryGroups: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs when their carriers
are available. None of the following headline theorems is statable at these pins
with only a few simple definitions:

* Adjacent invariant-distribution symmetry (README §2.2) needs test distributions
  on the local points of arbitrary Hermitian unitary groups.
* Bessel multiplicity one in every relevant odd codimension, its local reduction
  theorems and split generic nonvanishing (README §§2.3–2.6, 3.11) need the smooth
  admissible and Casselman–Wallach representation categories and their actual
  Bessel model spaces. Algebraic representations and intertwiners alone do not
  express these categories.
* Adjacent tempered integrability, regularized Bessel-form nonvanishing, geometric
  multiplicity and the local relative trace formula (README §§2.7, 3.3–3.5) need
  tempered representations, Harish–Chandra Schwartz spaces, quasi-characters and
  their germ coefficients on these groups.
* The epsilon character, its normalization transport, the component-character
  Fourier identity and the nonsplit tempered local GGP theorems (README
  §§3.1–3.2, 3.6–3.9) need actual unitary local parameters, their enhanced Langlands
  packets and normalized local root numbers. The real theta comparison also
  needs the oscillator representation and small theta lifts.
* Global period convergence and local factorization, and the tensor L-function
  comparison (README §§4.1–4.3), need cuspidal smooth automorphic realizations,
  their adelic Bessel periods, the unitary L-group and actual base change.
* The split Whittaker period identity, normalized local-form nonvanishing and
  spherical evaluation in every residue characteristic (README §§5.1a–5.3) need
  the smooth Whittaker realizations and local Rankin–Selberg, Asai and adjoint
  factors on the actual tempered representations.
* Global Whittaker-period factorization, the endoscopic spectral contribution,
  isolated relative comparison and the tempered relative-character Euler identity
  (README §§6.1–6.5) need induced automorphic
  realizations, their spectral contributions and relative-character distributions.
* Adjacent global nonvanishing, including its stable cuspidal specialization
  (README §§7.1–7.2), needs cuspidal automorphic representations of arbitrary-form
  unitary groups, actual base change, their adelic Bessel periods and completed
  Rankin–Selberg L-functions.
* The completed Tamagawa-normalized period identity GGP.8 (README §7.4) additionally
  needs the Petersson pairing, restricted smooth tensor factorization, normalized
  local period forms, Tamagawa measures and completed adjoint factors.

The split archimedean higher-codimension prediction (README §3.10) is a
conjectural proposition. The historically named fixed-pair global conjecture in
arbitrary odd codimension (README §4.4) is proved in the literature under the
discrete Hermitian base-change hypotheses compared there; its formal proof and
the additional Eisenstein-to-Bessel comparison belong to
GanGrossPrasadUnitaryGroups, Part II. Its actual cuspidal representation,
base-change and adelic Bessel-period carriers are also missing at the pins.
All these constructions remain specified in README.md. No auxiliary algebraic
identity substitutes for a headline theorem.
-/

